{"school":{"dbn":"02M542","name":"Manhattan Bridges High School","boro":"Manhattan","district":"02","district_label":"District 2","report_type":"HS","report_types":"HS","school_type":"High School","grades":"9 to 12","status":"open","enrollment":395,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"525 West 50Th Street","phone":"212-757-5274","website":"sites.google.com/manhattanbridgeshs.org/mbhs/home","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/high-school/65019","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Manhattan Bridges High School opened in September 2003 as a transitional bilingual school for Spanish-speaking students. Since 2007, the school has consistently received an \u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u009cA\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u009d on the NYC Progress Report. In 2009, the school introduced a dual language program for proficient English Speakers and the Academies of Engineering & Architecture Design, Computer Science, and Graphic Design, in collaboration with the National Action Council for Minorities in Engineering (NACME) and Project Lead the Way (PLTW). The college preparatory institution emphasizes the importance of mastering communication skills in both languages and offers ten Advanced Placement Courses (AP) Manhattan Bridges High School is part of the Career Readiness and Modern Youth Apprenticeship (CRMYA) pilot, offering ninth and tenth-graders courses to explore career interests and develop essential skills. Students can apply for apprenticeships in tech, finance, and business, allowing them to earn and learn while still in high school.","start_time":"08:20am","end_time":"03:10pm","languages":"Spanish","subway":"C, E to 50th St","bus":"M104, M11, M12, M20, M31, M34A-SBS, M42, M50, M57","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Clinton","latitude":40.7655,"longitude":-73.9927,"coordinate_source":"source","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_hs_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","202